                    full_text: "(1) Subject to the provisions of any Act of the National Assembly, the President of the National Industrial Court may make rules for regulating the practice and procedure of the National Industrial Court.\n\n(2) For the purpose of exercising its criminal jurisdiction, the provisions of the Criminal Code, Penal Code, Criminal Procedure Act, Criminal Procedure Code or Evidence Act shall apply.",
                    simple_summary: "The President of the National Industrial Court is responsible for writing the rules explaining how labor cases and trials are filed and processed.",
                    tags: ["court-rules", "procedures", "practice-directions", "industrial-court"]
